From ca89fb5fb96399ed730cacb12d948025f83c4e6e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Ukrainskiy <art.ukrainskiy@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 11:16:14 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Reduce forward substring setup cost and bound expensive
 comparisons

Use byte-sized Sunday shifts for short needles. For long scans, account for
failed partial comparisons and switch to bounded SIMD filters and Two-Way
when comparisons no longer pay for progress through the haystack.

Keep dispatch outside the comparison loops and retain the existing inline
memchr search. Add differential, binary and routing-boundary coverage for
the string APIs that share the forward matcher.
